{"id": "EUVD-2026-84220", "enisaUuid": "1e05edcc-c307-3429-a589-08354af2b801", "description": "vLLM through 0.29.0 fails to validate the tp_size parameter in kv_transfer_params on OpenAI-compatible completion endpoints, allowing attackers to allocate unbounded memory. Attackers can supply arbitrary tp_size values in prefill/decode disaggregated deployments to exhaust memory and trigger kernel OOM-kill of the decode worker process.", "datePublished": "2026-09-21T22:04:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T22:54:41", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51137", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.29.0/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/utils.py#L569-L573", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.29.0/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/metadata.py#L277", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-through-0.29.0-memory-exhaustion-via-unvalidated-nixl-tp-size"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-94626", "GHSA-hq63-vm56-2666", "PYSEC-2026-4008"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a31179a3-351c-38c9-ad2d-4530a24c74d3", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.29.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3bcb3211-91eb-3893-82cc-250a7854b902", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}